data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793218389827, "messageId": "59d3e96ae9", "delta": "If the reservoir were 10 °C colder, the **A1** design would still cover 100% of heating and cooling demands. However, the cost of heat would rise from **41 €/MWh** to **47.2 €/MWh**, and CO₂ savings against gas would drop from **82.2%** to **69.4%**.\\n\\nThe direct heat share from the doublet would decrease from 78.1% to 64.2%, while the heat pump contribution would increase from 19.5% to 25.7%. The peak boiler usage would also rise slightly from 2.5% to 10.1%.\\n\\nThese results come from mock tools and are marked as such."}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END", "timestamp": 1793218389827, "messageId": "59d3e96ae9"}

